{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790348156,"nonce":"Af+83fybR0r9TPvM9yZs8Ku+/XY=","title":"Ids in a loaded bytecode module can collide with ids minted afterwards","message":"max_hir_id (crates/compiler/src/bytecode.rs:837-864) does not visit HirEffectOp.id, the block ids inside HirEffectHandlerImpl.blocks, or HirVTable.id in constants, so after a load a newly minted HirId can equal one of them. Split images trust the writer's max_id (:527) instead of computing it.\n\nRelocation saturates silently (hir.rs:238-243): raw ids above u32::MAX - base all become u32::MAX with no error.\n\nTo confirm: LifetimeId and TypeId are neither relocated nor reserved on load (hir.rs:114-133; TypeId::reserve_at_least in typed_ast type_registry.rs:45 is never called from bytecode.rs), so a module loaded into a process that already minted those ids may alias them.","files":null}]}